<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19339" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gaulus</span></b> , i, m.
		Sanscr. gōlas, a waterpot; cf. also galley,
		galleon, = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γαυλός</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a pail</i>, 
			<i>round vessel</i>, <i><span class="en">Plaut. Rud.
				5, 2, 32</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A round merchant vessel</i>, = Gr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γαῦλος</span> (Hdt. 3, 136 sq.): genus navigii
			paene rotundum, Paul. ex <i><span class="en">Fest. p. 96</span></i> Müll.; cf.
				<i><span class="en">Gell. 10, 25, 5</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
